# Phonetic deploy commit messages

When creating git commits for this project (especially those that deploy to Vercel), prefix the subject line:

```
{word} - {summary}
```

- Use the **next word** from `.deploy-phonetic-next` (single lowercase line, e.g. `alpha`).
- After a successful commit, advance the file to the next NATO word: alpha → bravo → charlie → … → zulu → alpha.
- Include `.deploy-phonetic-next` in the same commit when it changes.
- Keep the summary after the dash in normal imperative style (e.g. `bravo - Fix supervisor scope sync on login`).

NATO sequence: alpha, bravo, charlie, delta, echo, foxtrot, golf, hotel, india, juliett, kilo, lima, mike, november, oscar, papa, quebec, romeo, sierra, tango, uniform, victor, whiskey, x-ray, yankee, zulu.

Do not skip letters or reuse a letter without advancing the tracker.
